    "policy_notes": [
      "Validated workflow specification LIONESS-DRAGON under project policy cf89ad9eddd6.",
      "Inputs are DRAGON's - two CSV or TSV tables with a header, the first column a unique sample ID and every other column a unique feature ID; rows are samples and columns are features in both layers.",
      "Layer 2 is reordered to layer 1 only after exact sample-ID set equality is proven. Values must be finite continuous numeric measurements; missing values, duplicate IDs and zero-variance features are rejected.",
      "Require at least three samples. The shrinkage values lambda1 and lambda2 are estimated once on all samples by estimate_penalty_parameters_dragon unless both are supplied in [0, 1].",
      "For sample k, LIONESS uses the all-sample DRAGON network and the network recomputed after removing k: N_k = n * (N_all - N_without_k) + N_without_k, as in netZooPy lioness/lioness_for_dragon.py.",
      "output_file is the labeled symmetric all-sample partial-correlation matrix; lioness_output is an edge-by-sample table with source, target and one column per sample, the upper triangle of each sample's matrix in DRAGON edge-list order.",
      "The per-sample table holds one value per feature pair per sample; runs above 20,000,000 values are refused before they start.",
      "Sample-specific networks are relative to the cohort they were built from; partial correlations are conditional associations, not causal relationships."
    ],
